---
import DocsNav from "../../components/DocsNav.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import { repositoryUrl } from "../../data/site";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Documentation | Loom Kernels"
  description="Contracts, integration, compatibility, and evidence for Loom Kernels."
>
  <header class="page-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
    <h1>Choose the boundary you need</h1>
    <p>
      Loom is an operator backend. The engine keeps tensors, streams, scheduling,
      GEMM, model state, and fallback policy.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="docs-layout">
    <DocsNav active="Start" />
    <article class="prose">
      <h2>Start here</h2>
      <div class="doc-grid">
        <div class="doc-card">
          <h3>Understand the design</h3>
          <p>Read the product boundary, execution path, and admission gates.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/design/operator-library.md`}>Operator-library design</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <h3>Integrate an engine</h3>
          <p>Build the native wheel and enable only measured PyTorch or vLLM routes.</p>
          <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}docs/integration/`}>Integration guide</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <h3>Check compatibility</h3>
          <p>Confirm the CUDA, PyTorch, vLLM, Python, and bridge ABI boundary.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/compatibility.md`}>Compatibility matrix</a>
        </div>
        <div class="doc-card">
          <h3>Inspect results</h3>
          <p>Read accepted, parity, fallback, and rejected H20 evidence.</p>
          <a href={`${repositoryUrl}/blob/main/docs/results/README.md`}>Evidence index</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <h2>Validate the Rust workspace</h2>
      <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/feichai0017/loom-kernels.git
cd loom-kernels
cargo fmt --all -- --check
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo test --workspace --all-targets</code></pre>

      <h2>Repository layers</h2>
      <table class="operator-table">
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Path</th><th>Responsibility</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>loom-kernels</td><td>Contracts, capabilities, and CPU oracles.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>loom-cuda</td><td>Safe memory, stream, layout, and dispatch APIs.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>loom-cuda-bridge</td><td>Checked framework boundary.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>loom-cuda-sys</td><td>Internal CUDA ABI and kernels.</td></tr>
          <tr><td>python</td><td>Stable ABI PyTorch operators and vLLM policy.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <div class="doc-note">
        <strong>Evidence is cumulative.</strong>
        <p>
          Contract, CUDA, benchmark, framework, engine, and system gates are
          separate. Passing one does not imply the next.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
